                            <p></p><h3>Definition of "ecc803s":</h3><p><b>ECC803S</b> was Telefunken&#8217;s model name for a high-grade 12AX7-style dual-triode vacuum tube. It is considered by many audio engineers to be the finest triode available, in part because it was specified for a 10,000-hour service life.</p><p><img src="/images/tubes/ecc803s.jpg" width="100" alt="Telefunken ECC803S" class="thumb shaft" />The Telefunken ECC803S was a &#8220;frame grid&#8221; tube; the use of a frame grid allowed for shorter, finer wires inside the tube, resulting in a reduction of noise even at very high gain.</p><p>The tube was built with gold pins, to improve its electrical connection.</p><p>Read more about <a href="http://www.jacmusic.com/nos/ECC83-part-numbering1.html">ECC803S frame-grid tubes</a>.</p>
